  "verbalization": "Delta-Selinene appears to interact with Granzyme B through a series of molecular pathways, with ME-180 acting as a central mediator. The evidence suggests that delta-Selinene targets ME-180, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Chikusetsusaponin Iva and 2',4'-Dihydroxydihydrochalcone, all of which ultimately lead to Granzyme B. This indicates a potential cascade of interactions where delta-Selinene may influence Granzyme B via ME-180, possibly through the activation of downstream signaling pathways. The presence of multiple overlapping targets, including Npc199963, further supports the idea that ME-180 is a key node in this network. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of ME-180 as a common intermediary, suggesting that delta-Selinene may exert its effects on Granzyme B through a shared mechanism involving ME-180. The evidence is consistent with a model where delta-Selinene modulates Granzyme B via ME-180, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
